# Squire Docs self-host settings.
#
# This file is a menu, not your configuration. Copy any line you want into
# .env in this folder, remove the leading "# ", set the value, then run:
#   docker compose up -d --wait
# Nothing here is required. A fresh install runs in local mode: one owner
# account, signed in with a link from ./squire claim-link, no password and no
# sign-up page.

# Host port for the web app, if 3910 is taken.
# SQUIRE_PORT=3910

# The release this folder runs. install.sh writes it to .env. To upgrade, set
# it to the new release, then run: docker compose pull && docker compose up -d --wait
SQUIRE_VERSION=__SQUIRE_VERSION__

# Instance mode. Local mode is the default; team mode arrives in a later release.
# SQUIRE_MODE=local

# Assistant keys (server-wide). Without one, the in-app assistant asks each
# person for their own key in Settings. Your own agent connected over MCP
# needs no key here.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Semantic search and the Gemini assistant models. Without it, search uses
# full-text matching only.
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# Email. Without SMTP_HOST, Squire Docs sends no email. Port 465 uses implicit
# TLS; any other port uses STARTTLS unless SMTP_SECURE says otherwise.
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=465
# SMTP_SECURE=
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# SMTP_FROM=

# Images. The default stores image bytes in the squire-data volume. Set the S3
# lines to use S3 or an S3-compatible service such as MinIO (S3_ENDPOINT).
# STORAGE_DRIVER=local
# S3_IMAGE_BUCKET=
# S3_IMAGE_REGION=us-east-1
# S3_ENDPOINT=
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Public URL. Derived from SQUIRE_PORT as http://localhost:<port>. Plain HTTP
# is supported only on localhost: to expose this instance, put a TLS-terminating
# proxy in front of it and set an https URL here.
# APP_URL=https://docs.example.com

# The full list of settings is in the configuration table of the Squire Docs
# README, and https://squiredocs.com/documentation/self-hosting explains these.
